config BR2_PACKAGE_ATV1_CLIENT
	bool "atv1-client (prebuilt Rust appliance client)"
	help
	  The Rust appliance control-surface binary (ARCHITECTURE
	  doc §1-§4): full-screen update flow, coordinator agent,
	  Kodi handoff adapter. Rust-only application code is the
	  project convention; Buildroot 2017.08-era has no Rust
	  toolchain, so the binary is cross-built against this
	  system's SDK out-of-era (tools/build-client.sh) and is
	  installed from the convention path:

	    $(BR2_EXTERNAL_ATV1_PATH)/client/atv1-client

  post-build.sh installs it there when this option is enabled.
  Startup model (headless agent vs tty1 kiosk replacing
  startkodi.sh) is an open ARCHITECTURE decision (§8) — until
  it is made, startkodi.sh keeps the kiosk and the client runs
  as a managed service only.
